      "side": 1,
      "message": "This obviously makes the assumption that the \"notifier_subscriptions\" field is the first field in the \"_hdr\" struct. Please add a comment here and in the struct definition calling out this assumption. The obvious question is why do we need to make this assumption instead of using something like container_of() -- the issue is that the visibility causes CRC issues, so explain that.",
